IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc26-interpretation`

-- ccc26-fines.l4 -- sections 734 to 736 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: fines and forfeiture (lines 15645-15768 of the text).
-- Layer 1 of part ccc26. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text. Section 734.8(1) ("penalty") and the `Fine` answer the other parts ask for are in
-- ccc26-interpretation. Money is in dollars; the provincial minimum hourly wage and the costs and charges (set by provincial regulations) are inputs.

§ `Section 734 -- Power of court to impose fine`

-- (1): the power to fine. "Subject to subsection (2)": that subsection is its own function below.
-- src:15645 | Fines and Forfeiture
-- src:15646 | Power of court to impose fine
-- src:15647 | 734 (1) Subject to subsection (2), a court that convicts a person, other than an organization, of an offence may fine the offender by making an order under section 734.1
-- src:15648 | (a) if the punishment for the offence does not include a minimum term of imprisonment, in addition to or in lieu of any other sanction that the court is authorized to impose; or
-- src:15649 | (b) if the punishment for the offence includes a minimum term of imprisonment, in addition to any other sanction that the court is required or authorized to impose.
@ref s 734(1) (src:15645-15649)
GIVEN `the court convicts a person of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the punishment for the offence includes a minimum term of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine would be imposed in lieu of any other sanction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734(1) the court may fine the offender by making an order under section 734.1` MEANS   -- gate: none (the limits are on whose case and on the fine in lieu of another sanction)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court convicts a person of an offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a court that convicts a person, other than an organization, of an offence may fine the offender"
        IF `the person is an organization` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than an organization"
        IF `the punishment for the offence includes a minimum term of imprisonment` AND `the fine would be imposed in lieu of any other sanction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the punishment for the offence includes a minimum term of imprisonment, in addition to any other sanction that the court is required or authorized to impose"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2): the ability-to-pay bar, closed by "only if" and opened by "Except when".
-- src:15650 | Offender’s ability to pay
-- src:15651 | (2) Except when the punishment for an offence includes a minimum fine or a fine is imposed in lieu of a forfeiture order, a court may fine an offender under this section only if the court is satisfied that the offender is able to pay the fine or discharge it under section 736.
@ref s 734(2) (src:15650-15651)
GIVEN `the punishment for the offence includes a minimum fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine is imposed in lieu of a forfeiture order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the offender is able to pay the fine or discharge it under section 736` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734(2) the ability-to-pay condition bars the fine` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the punishment for the offence includes a minimum fine` OR `the fine is imposed in lieu of a forfeiture order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except when the punishment for an offence includes a minimum fine or a fine is imposed in lieu of a forfeiture order"
        IF `the court is satisfied that the offender is able to pay the fine or discharge it under section 736` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if the court is satisfied that the offender is able to pay the fine or discharge it under section 736"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3): default of payment.
-- src:15652 | Meaning of default of payment
-- src:15653 | (3) For the purposes of this section and sections 734.1 to 737, a person is in default of payment of a fine if the fine has not been paid in full by the time set out in the order made under section 734.1.
@ref s 734(3) (src:15652-15653)
GIVEN `the fine has been paid in full by the time set out in the order made under section 734.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734(3) the person is in default of payment of the fine` MEANS
    IF `the fine has been paid in full by the time set out in the order made under section 734.1`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is in default of payment of a fine if the fine has not been paid in full by the time set out in the order"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (4): the deemed term.
-- src:15654 | Imprisonment in default of payment
-- src:15655 | (4) Where an offender is fined under this section, a term of imprisonment, determined in accordance with subsection (5), shall be deemed to be imposed in default of payment of the fine.
@ref s 734(4) (src:15654-15655)
GIVEN `the offender is fined under section 734` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734(4) a term of imprisonment is deemed to be imposed in default of payment of the fine` MEANS
    IF `the offender is fined under section 734`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an offender is fined under this section, a term of imprisonment, determined in accordance with subsection (5), shall be deemed to be imposed in default of payment of the fine"

-- (5): the term. (a) is the number of days that a fraction, rounded down, gives; (b) is the longest term the court could itself impose or, where the punishment includes
-- no term of imprisonment, five years (indictable) or two years less a day (summary conviction). The days in a Length of time depend on the date it runs from, so (b) takes the
-- date of default as the anchor. `no imprisonment is stated` is read as "the punishment does not include a term of imprisonment"; life imprisonment leaves (b) without a ceiling.
-- src:15656 | Determination of term
-- src:15657 | (5) The term of imprisonment referred to in subsection (4) is the lesser of
-- src:15658 | (a) the number of days that corresponds to a fraction, rounded down to the nearest whole number, of which
-- src:15659 | (i) the numerator is the unpaid amount of the fine plus the costs and charges of committing and conveying the defaulter to prison, calculated in accordance with regulations made under subsection (7), and
-- src:15660 | (ii) the denominator is equal to eight times the provincial minimum hourly wage, at the time of default, in the province in which the fine was imposed, and
-- src:15661 | (b) the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction or, if the punishment for the offence does not include a term of imprisonment, five years in the case of an indictable offence or two years less a day in the case of a summary conviction offence.
@ref s 734(5) (src:15656-15661)
GIVEN term IS A `Length of time`
      `the date of default` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 734(5)(b) the number of days in the term counted from the date of default` MEANS
    (`Date to days` (`add months` `the date of default` (`s 716 the months in the period` term))) MINUS (`Date to days` `the date of default`) PLUS term's days MINUS (IF term's `less a day` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

@ref s 734(5)(a) (src:15658-15660)
GIVEN `the unpaid amount of the fine` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs and charges of committing and conveying the defaulter to prison, calculated in accordance with regulations made under subsection 734(7)` IS A NUMBER
      `the provincial minimum hourly wage, at the time of default, in the province in which the fine was imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 734(5)(a) the number of days that corresponds to the fraction, rounded down to the nearest whole number` MEANS
    IF `the provincial minimum hourly wage, at the time of default, in the province in which the fine was imposed` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the provincial minimum hourly wage is not a positive amount, so the fraction has no value
    ELSE JUST (FLOOR ((`the unpaid amount of the fine` PLUS `the costs and charges of committing and conveying the defaulter to prison, calculated in accordance with regulations made under subsection 734(7)`) DIVIDED BY (8 TIMES `the provincial minimum hourly wage, at the time of default, in the province in which the fine was imposed`)))

@ref s 734(5)(b) (src:15661)
GIVEN `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the offence is proceeded with by` IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `the date of default` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 734(5)(b) the maximum number of days of the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction`
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): imprisonment for life gives paragraph (b) no ceiling in days
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN JUST (`s 734(5)(b) the number of days in the term counted from the date of default` term `the date of default`)
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN
        CONSIDER `the offence is proceeded with by`
        WHEN `by indictment` THEN JUST (`s 734(5)(b) the number of days in the term counted from the date of default` `five years` `the date of default`)
        WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (`s 734(5)(b) the number of days in the term counted from the date of default` `two years less a day` `the date of default`)

@ref s 734(5) (src:15656-15661)
GIVEN `the unpaid amount of the fine` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs and charges of committing and conveying the defaulter to prison, calculated in accordance with regulations made under subsection 734(7)` IS A NUMBER
      `the provincial minimum hourly wage, at the time of default, in the province in which the fine was imposed` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the offence is proceeded with by` IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `the date of default` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 734(5) the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine, in days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 734(5)(a) the number of days that corresponds to the fraction, rounded down to the nearest whole number` `the unpaid amount of the fine` `the costs and charges of committing and conveying the defaulter to prison, calculated in accordance with regulations made under subsection 734(7)` `the provincial minimum hourly wage, at the time of default, in the province in which the fine was imposed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): paragraph (a) has no value
    WHEN JUST fraction THEN
        CONSIDER `s 734(5)(b) the maximum number of days of the term` `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction` `the offence is proceeded with by` `the date of default`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST fraction   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): imprisonment for life leaves only paragraph (a)
        WHEN JUST ceiling THEN JUST (IF fraction AT MOST ceiling THEN fraction ELSE ceiling)

-- (6): moneys found on the offender. A grant with an "if" gate: NOTHING where it is not met.
-- src:15662 | Moneys found on offender
-- src:15663 | (6) All or any part of a fine imposed under this section may be taken out of moneys found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest of the offender if the court making the order, on being satisfied that ownership of or right to possession of those moneys is not disputed by claimants other than the offender, so directs.
@ref s 734(6) (src:15662-15663)
GIVEN `the fine was imposed under section 734` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moneys were found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that ownership of or right to possession of those moneys is not disputed by claimants other than the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court so directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734(6) all or any part of the fine may be taken out of the moneys found` MEANS   -- gate: if (the court, on being satisfied that ownership is not disputed by claimants other than the offender, so directs)
    IF `the fine was imposed under section 734` AND `the moneys were found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest of the offender` AND `the court is satisfied that ownership of or right to possession of those moneys is not disputed by claimants other than the offender` AND `the court so directs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be taken out of moneys found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest of the offender if the court making the order, on being satisfied that ownership of or right to possession of those moneys is not disputed by claimants other than the offender, so directs"

-- (7) is a provincial regulation-making power (inert, reason 2).
-- (8): the reach of ss 734 to 734.8 and 736, with the exception for the term in default.
-- src:15666 | Application to other law
-- src:15667 | (8) This section and sections 734.1 to 734.8 and 736 apply to a fine imposed under any Act of Parliament, except that subsections (4) and (5) do not apply if the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine provided for in that Act or regulation is
-- src:15668 | (a) calculated by a different method; or
-- src:15669 | (b) specified, either as a minimum or a maximum.
@ref s 734(8) (src:15666-15669)
GIVEN `the fine is imposed under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine provided for in that Act or regulation is calculated by a different method` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine provided for in that Act or regulation is specified, either as a minimum or a maximum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734(8) subsections 734(4) and (5) apply to the fine` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the fine is imposed under an Act of Parliament` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to a fine imposed under any Act of Parliament"
        IF `the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine provided for in that Act or regulation is calculated by a different method` OR `the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine provided for in that Act or regulation is specified, either as a minimum or a maximum` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that subsections (4) and (5) do not apply if the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine provided for in that Act or regulation is (a) calculated by a different method; or (b) specified, either as a minimum or a maximum"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Sections 734.1 to 734.3 -- Terms of order imposing fine; obligations of court; change in terms`

-- 734.1: "shall do so by making an order that clearly sets out (a) ... (d)". Paragraph (d) is a set of terms the court deems appropriate.
-- src:15670 | Terms of order imposing fine
-- src:15671 | 734.1 A court that fines an offender under section 734 shall do so by making an order that clearly sets out
-- src:15672 | (a) the amount of the fine;
-- src:15673 | (b) the manner in which the fine is to be paid;
-- src:15674 | (c) the time or times by which the fine, or any portion thereof, must be paid; and
-- src:15675 | (d) such other terms respecting the payment of the fine as the court deems appropriate.
@ref s 734.1 (src:15670-15675)
GIVEN `the court fines an offender under section 734` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order clearly sets out the amount of the fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order clearly sets out the manner in which the fine is to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order clearly sets out the time or times by which the fine, or any portion thereof, must be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court deems other terms respecting the payment of the fine appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order clearly sets out those other terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.1 the order clearly sets out the terms the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court fines an offender under section 734` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that fines an offender under section 734 shall do so by making an order"
        IF `the order clearly sets out the amount of the fine` AND `the order clearly sets out the manner in which the fine is to be paid` AND `the order clearly sets out the time or times by which the fine, or any portion thereof, must be paid` AND ((NOT `the court deems other terms respecting the payment of the fine appropriate`) OR `the order clearly sets out those other terms`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall do so by making an order that clearly sets out (a) the amount of the fine; (b) the manner in which the fine is to be paid; (c) the time or times by which the fine, or any portion thereof, must be paid; and (d) such other terms respecting the payment of the fine as the court deems appropriate"

-- src:15676 | Obligations of court
-- src:15677 | 734.2 (1) A court that makes an order under section 734.1 shall
-- src:15678 | (a) cause a copy of the order to be given to the offender;
-- src:15679 | (b) explain the substance of sections 734 to 734.8 and 736 to the offender;
-- src:15680 | (c) cause an explanation to be given to the offender of the procedure for applying under section 734.3 for a change to the optional conditions and of any available fine option programs referred to in section 736 as well as the procedure to apply for admission to them; and
-- src:15681 | (d) take reasonable measures to ensure that the offender understands the order and the explanations.
@ref s 734.2(1) (src:15676-15681)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under section 734.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.2(1)(a) the court must cause a copy of the order to be given to the offender` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under section 734.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that makes an order under section 734.1 shall"

@ref s 734.2(1)(b) (src:15676-15679)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under section 734.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.2(1)(b) the court must explain the substance of sections 734 to 734.8 and 736 to the offender` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under section 734.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that makes an order under section 734.1 shall"

@ref s 734.2(1)(c) (src:15676-15680)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under section 734.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.2(1)(c) the court must cause an explanation to be given to the offender of the procedure for applying for a change and of any available fine option programs` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under section 734.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that makes an order under section 734.1 shall"

@ref s 734.2(1)(d) (src:15676-15681)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under section 734.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.2(1)(d) the court must take reasonable measures to ensure that the offender understands the order and the explanations` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under section 734.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that makes an order under section 734.1 shall"

-- src:15682 | For greater certainty
-- src:15683 | (2) For greater certainty, a failure to comply with subsection (1) does not affect the validity of the order.
@ref s 734.2(2) (src:15682-15683)
GIVEN `the court failed to comply with subsection 734.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.2(2) the failure leaves the validity of the order unaffected` MEANS
    IF `the court failed to comply with subsection 734.2(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a failure to comply with subsection (1) does not affect the validity of the order"

-- 734.3: change in the terms of an order, "on application", "except the amount of the fine".
-- src:15684 | Change in terms of order
-- src:15685 | 734.3 A court that makes an order under section 734.1, or a person designated either by name or by title of office by that court, may, on application by or on behalf of the offender, subject to any rules made by the court under section 482 or 482.1, change any term of the order except the amount of the fine, and any reference in this section and sections 734, 734.1, 734.2 and 734.6 to an order shall be read as including a reference to the order as changed under this section.
@ref s 734.3 (src:15684-15685)
GIVEN `the person is a court that makes an order under section 734.1 or a person designated either by name or by title of office by that court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender or a person on the offender's behalf applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term to be changed is the amount of the fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a rule made by the court under section 482 or 482.1 bars the change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.3 the court or its designate may change the term of the order` MEANS   -- gate: on (application by or on behalf of the offender); closed exception (the amount of the fine)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is a court that makes an order under section 734.1 or a person designated either by name or by title of office by that court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that makes an order under section 734.1, or a person designated either by name or by title of office by that court, may"
        IF NOT `the offender or a person on the offender's behalf applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application by or on behalf of the offender"
        IF `the term to be changed is the amount of the fine` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "change any term of the order except the amount of the fine"
        IF `a rule made by the court under section 482 or 482.1 bars the change` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any rules made by the court under section 482 or 482.1"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Sections 734.4 and 734.5 -- Proceeds of fines; licences, permits, etc.`

-- 734.4(1) and (2): whose the proceeds are. The proceeds described in (1) belong to the province unless (2) gives them to Canada.
-- src:15686 | Proceeds to go to provincial treasurer
-- src:15687 | 734.4 (1) If a fine or forfeiture is imposed or an amount set out in an undertaking, release order or recognizance is forfeited and no provision, other than this section, is made by law for the application of the proceeds, the proceeds belong to Her Majesty in right of the province in which the fine or forfeiture was imposed or the amount was forfeited, and shall be paid by the person who receives them to the treasurer of that province.
-- src:15688 | Proceeds to go to Receiver General for Canada
-- src:15689 | (2) The proceeds described in subsection (1) belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada and must be paid by the person who receives them to the Receiver General if, as the case may be,
-- src:15690 | (a) the fine or forfeiture is imposed
-- src:15691 | (i) in respect of a contravention of a revenue law of Canada,
-- src:15692 | (ii) in respect of a breach of duty or malfeasance in office by an officer or employee of the Government of Canada, or
-- src:15693 | (iii) in respect of any proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada in which that government bears the costs of prosecution; or
-- src:15694 | (b) an amount set out in an undertaking, release order or recognizance is forfeited in connection with proceedings mentioned in paragraph (a).
@ref s 734.4(2) (src:15686-15694)
DECLARE `s 734.4 owner of the proceeds` IS ONE OF
    `s 734.4(1) Her Majesty in right of the province in which the fine or forfeiture was imposed or the amount was forfeited`
    `s 734.4(2) Her Majesty in right of Canada`

@ref s 734.4(1) (src:15686-15687)
GIVEN `a fine or forfeiture is imposed or an amount set out in an undertaking, release order or recognizance is forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no provision, other than section 734.4, is made by law for the application of the proceeds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine or forfeiture is imposed in respect of a contravention of a revenue law of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine or forfeiture is imposed in respect of a breach of duty or malfeasance in office by an officer or employee of the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine or forfeiture is imposed in respect of any proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada in which that government bears the costs of prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an amount set out in an undertaking, release order or recognizance is forfeited in connection with proceedings of one of those kinds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 734.4 owner of the proceeds`
`s 734.4 whose the proceeds are` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a fine or forfeiture is imposed or an amount set out in an undertaking, release order or recognizance is forfeited` AND `no provision, other than section 734.4, is made by law for the application of the proceeds`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a fine or forfeiture is imposed or an amount set out in an undertaking, release order or recognizance is forfeited and no provision, other than this section, is made by law for the application of the proceeds, the proceeds belong to Her Majesty in right of the province"
        IF `the fine or forfeiture is imposed in respect of a contravention of a revenue law of Canada` OR `the fine or forfeiture is imposed in respect of a breach of duty or malfeasance in office by an officer or employee of the Government of Canada` OR `the fine or forfeiture is imposed in respect of any proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada in which that government bears the costs of prosecution` OR `an amount set out in an undertaking, release order or recognizance is forfeited in connection with proceedings of one of those kinds` THEN JUST `s 734.4(2) Her Majesty in right of Canada`
        OTHERWISE JUST `s 734.4(1) Her Majesty in right of the province in which the fine or forfeiture was imposed or the amount was forfeited`

-- src:15695 | Direction for payment to municipality
-- src:15696 | (3) If a provincial, municipal or local authority bears, in whole or in part, the expense of administering the law under which a fine or forfeiture is imposed or under which proceedings are taken in which an amount set out in an undertaking, release order or recognizance is forfeited,
-- src:15697 | (a) the lieutenant governor in council of a province may direct that the proceeds that belong to Her Majesty in right of the province shall be paid to that authority; and
-- src:15698 | (b) the Governor in Council may direct that the proceeds that belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada shall be paid to that authority.
-- src:15699 | Licences, permits, etc.
@ref s 734.4(3) (src:15695-15699)
GIVEN `a provincial, municipal or local authority bears, in whole or in part, the expense of administering the law under which a fine or forfeiture is imposed or proceedings are taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeds belong to Her Majesty in right of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.4(3)(a) the lieutenant governor in council of a province may direct that the proceeds be paid to that authority` MEANS   -- gate: if (a provincial, municipal or local authority bears the expense)
    IF `a provincial, municipal or local authority bears, in whole or in part, the expense of administering the law under which a fine or forfeiture is imposed or proceedings are taken` AND `the proceeds belong to Her Majesty in right of the province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the lieutenant governor in council of a province may direct that the proceeds that belong to Her Majesty in right of the province shall be paid to that authority"

@ref s 734.4(3)(b) (src:15695-15699)
GIVEN `a provincial, municipal or local authority bears, in whole or in part, the expense of administering the law under which a fine or forfeiture is imposed or proceedings are taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeds belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.4(3)(b) the Governor in Council may direct that the proceeds be paid to that authority` MEANS   -- gate: if (a provincial, municipal or local authority bears the expense)
    IF `a provincial, municipal or local authority bears, in whole or in part, the expense of administering the law under which a fine or forfeiture is imposed or proceedings are taken` AND `the proceeds belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Governor in Council may direct that the proceeds that belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada shall be paid to that authority"

-- 734.5: licences, permits and similar instruments. Paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) pair who owns the proceeds with who issues the instrument.
-- src:15700 | 734.5 If an offender is in default of payment of a fine,
-- src:15701 | (a) where the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of a province by virtue of subsection 734.4(1), the person responsible, by or under an Act of the legislature of the province, for issuing, renewing or suspending a licence, permit or other similar instrument in relation to the offender may refuse to issue or renew or may suspend the licence, permit or other instrument until the fine is paid in full, proof of which lies on the offender;
-- src:15702 | (b) where the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada by virtue of subsection 734.4(2), the person responsible, by or under an Act of Parliament, for issuing or renewing a licence, permit or other similar instrument in relation to the offender may refuse to issue or renew or may suspend the licence, permit or other instrument until the fine is paid in full, proof of which lies on the offender; or
-- src:15703 | (c) where the proceeds of the fine belong to His Majesty in right of Canada by virtue of subsection 734.4(2), the person responsible, by or under an Act of the legislature of a province, for issuing, renewing or suspending a licence, permit or other similar instrument in relation to the offender may refuse to issue or renew or may suspend the licence, permit or other instrument until the fine is paid in full, proof of which lies on the offender.
@ref s 734.5 (src:15700-15703)
GIVEN `the offender is in default of payment of a fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of a province by virtue of subsection 734.4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada by virtue of subsection 734.4(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is responsible, by or under an Act of the legislature of a province, for issuing, renewing or suspending a licence, permit or other similar instrument in relation to the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is responsible, by or under an Act of Parliament, for issuing or renewing a licence, permit or other similar instrument in relation to the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.5 the person responsible may refuse to issue or renew or may suspend the licence, permit or other instrument until the fine is paid in full` MEANS   -- gate: if (the offender is in default of payment of a fine), where (the proceeds belong to Her Majesty in right of a province or of Canada)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offender is in default of payment of a fine` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an offender is in default of payment of a fine"
        IF NOT (`the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of a province by virtue of subsection 734.4(1)` OR `the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada by virtue of subsection 734.4(2)`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of a province by virtue of subsection 734.4(1)"
        IF `the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of a province by virtue of subsection 734.4(1)` AND `the person is responsible, by or under an Act of the legislature of a province, for issuing, renewing or suspending a licence, permit or other similar instrument in relation to the offender` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada by virtue of subsection 734.4(2)` AND `the person is responsible, by or under an Act of Parliament, for issuing or renewing a licence, permit or other similar instrument in relation to the offender` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada by virtue of subsection 734.4(2)` AND `the person is responsible, by or under an Act of the legislature of a province, for issuing, renewing or suspending a licence, permit or other similar instrument in relation to the offender` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person responsible, by or under an Act of the legislature of the province, for issuing, renewing or suspending a licence, permit or other similar instrument in relation to the offender may refuse to issue or renew or may suspend the licence, permit or other instrument until the fine is paid in full"

-- 734.51 (agreements between the Attorney General of Canada and a province) is machinery (inert, reason 2).
§ `Section 734.6 -- Civil enforcement of fines, forfeiture`

-- src:15710 | Civil enforcement of fines, forfeiture
-- src:15711 | 734.6 (1) Where
-- src:15712 | (a) an offender is in default of payment of a fine, or
-- src:15713 | (b) a forfeiture imposed by law is not paid as required by the order imposing it,
-- src:15714 | then, in addition to any other method provided by law for recovering the fine or forfeiture,
-- src:15715 | (c) the Attorney General of the province to whom the proceeds of the fine or forfeiture belong, or
-- src:15716 | (d) the Attorney General of Canada, where the proceeds of the fine or forfeiture belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada,
-- src:15717 | may, by filing the order, enter as a judgment the amount of the fine or forfeiture, and costs, if any, in any civil court in Canada that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount.
@ref s 734.6(1) (src:15710-15717)
GIVEN `the offender is in default of payment of a fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a forfeiture imposed by law is not paid as required by the order imposing it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Attorney General of the province to whom the proceeds of the fine or forfeiture belong` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Attorney General of Canada and the proceeds of the fine or forfeiture belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the civil court has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.6(1) the Attorney General may enter the amount of the fine or forfeiture, and costs, as a judgment in a civil court by filing the order` MEANS   -- gate: where (the offender is in default of payment of a fine, or a forfeiture imposed by law is not paid as required)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offender is in default of payment of a fine` OR `a forfeiture imposed by law is not paid as required by the order imposing it`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where (a) an offender is in default of payment of a fine, or (b) a forfeiture imposed by law is not paid as required by the order imposing it"
        IF NOT (`the person is the Attorney General of the province to whom the proceeds of the fine or forfeiture belong` OR `the person is the Attorney General of Canada and the proceeds of the fine or forfeiture belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) the Attorney General of the province to whom the proceeds of the fine or forfeiture belong, or (d) the Attorney General of Canada, where the proceeds of the fine or forfeiture belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada, may"
        IF NOT `the civil court has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any civil court in Canada that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15718 | Effect of filing order
-- src:15719 | (2) An order that is entered as a judgment under this section is enforceable in the same manner as if it were a judgment obtained by the Attorney General of the province or the Attorney General of Canada, as the case may be, in civil proceedings.
@ref s 734.6(2) (src:15718-15719)
GIVEN `the order is entered as a judgment under section 734.6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.6(2) the entered order is enforceable in the same manner as a judgment obtained by the Attorney General in civil proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the order is entered as a judgment under section 734.6`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order that is entered as a judgment under this section is enforceable in the same manner as if it were a judgment obtained by the Attorney General"

§ `Section 734.7 -- Warrant of committal`

-- (1): a flat negative with "until" and "unless": barred until the time for payment has expired, and then barred unless the court is satisfied of (i) or (ii).
-- The bar is also a SHANT rule, with the number of days of the time allowed as an input.
-- src:15720 | Warrant of committal
-- src:15721 | 734.7 (1) Where time has been allowed for payment of a fine, the court shall not issue a warrant of committal in default of payment of the fine
-- src:15722 | (a) until the expiration of the time allowed for payment of the fine in full; and
-- src:15723 | (b) unless the court is satisfied
-- src:15724 | (i) that the mechanisms provided by sections 734.5 and 734.6 are not appropriate in the circumstances, or
-- src:15725 | (ii) that the offender has, without reasonable excuse, refused to pay the fine or discharge it under section 736.
@ref s 734.7(1) (src:15720-15725)
GIVEN `time has been allowed for payment of the fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time allowed for payment of the fine in full has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the mechanisms provided by sections 734.5 and 734.6 are not appropriate in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the offender has, without reasonable excuse, refused to pay the fine or discharge it under section 736` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.7(1) the court is barred from issuing a warrant of committal in default of payment of the fine` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `time has been allowed for payment of the fine` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where time has been allowed for payment of a fine, the court shall not issue a warrant of committal"
        IF NOT `the time allowed for payment of the fine in full has expired` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the court is satisfied that the mechanisms provided by sections 734.5 and 734.6 are not appropriate in the circumstances` OR `the court is satisfied that the offender has, without reasonable excuse, refused to pay the fine or discharge it under section 736` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court is satisfied (i) that the mechanisms provided by sections 734.5 and 734.6 are not appropriate in the circumstances, or (ii) that the offender has, without reasonable excuse, refused to pay the fine or discharge it under section 736"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 734.7(1)(a) (src:15720-15722)
DECLARE `s 734.7(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 734.7(1) issue a warrant of committal in default of payment of the fine`

@ref s 734.7(1)(a) (src:15720-15722)
GIVEN `time has been allowed for payment of the fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of the time allowed for payment of the fine in full` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 734.7(1) action`
`s 734.7(1) the court's duty not to issue a warrant of committal before the time for payment has expired` MEANS
    IF `time has been allowed for payment of the fine`
    THEN PARTY `the court` SHANT `s 734.7(1) issue a warrant of committal in default of payment of the fine`
         WITHIN `the number of days of the time allowed for payment of the fine in full`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court issued a warrant of committal before the expiration of the time allowed for payment of the fine in full"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:15726 | Reasons for committal
-- src:15727 | (2) Where no time has been allowed for payment of a fine and a warrant committing the offender to prison for default of payment of the fine is issued, the court shall state in the warrant the reason for immediate committal.
@ref s 734.7(2) (src:15726-15727)
GIVEN `no time has been allowed for payment of the fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warrant committing the offender to prison for default of payment of the fine is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.7(2) the court must state in the warrant the reason for immediate committal` MEANS
    IF `no time has been allowed for payment of the fine` AND `a warrant committing the offender to prison for default of payment of the fine is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where no time has been allowed for payment of a fine and a warrant committing the offender to prison for default of payment of the fine is issued, the court shall state in the warrant the reason for immediate committal"

-- src:15728 | Period of imprisonment
-- src:15729 | (2.1) The period of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine shall be specified in a warrant of committal referred to in subsection (1) or (2).
@ref s 734.7(2.1) (src:15728-15729)
GIVEN `the warrant is a warrant of committal referred to in subsection 734.7(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.7(2.1) the warrant must specify the period of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine` MEANS
    IF `the warrant is a warrant of committal referred to in subsection 734.7(1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be specified in a warrant of committal referred to in subsection (1) or (2)"

-- src:15730 | Compelling appearance of person bound
-- src:15731 | (3) The provisions of Parts XVI and XVIII with respect to compelling the appearance of an accused before a justice apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to proceedings under paragraph (1)(b).
@ref s 734.7(3) (src:15730-15731)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a proceeding under paragraph 734.7(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.7(3) the provisions of Parts XVI and XVIII for compelling the appearance of an accused apply to the proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is a proceeding under paragraph 734.7(1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to proceedings under paragraph (1)(b)"

-- src:15732 | Effect of imprisonment
-- src:15733 | (4) The imprisonment of an offender for default of payment of a fine terminates the operation of sections 734.5 and 734.6 in relation to that fine.
@ref s 734.7(4) (src:15732-15733)
GIVEN `the offender is imprisoned for default of payment of the fine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.7(4) the imprisonment terminates the operation of sections 734.5 and 734.6 in relation to the fine` MEANS
    IF `the offender is imprisoned for default of payment of the fine`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The imprisonment of an offender for default of payment of a fine terminates the operation of sections 734.5 and 734.6 in relation to that fine"

§ `Section 734.8 -- Part payment and application of money paid`

-- (2): the reduction of the term on part payment, in days. The text gives the proportion and no rule for rounding.
-- src:15738 | Reduction of imprisonment on part payment
-- src:15739 | (2) The term of imprisonment in default of payment of a fine shall, on payment of a part of the penalty, whether the payment was made before or after the execution of a warrant of committal, be reduced by the number of days that bears the same proportion to the number of days in the term as the part paid bears to the total penalty.
@ref s 734.8(2) (src:15738-15739)
GIVEN `the number of days in the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the penalty paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the total penalty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 734.8(2) the number of days by which the term is reduced` MEANS
    IF `the total penalty` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): there is no total penalty to take a proportion of
    ELSE JUST ((`the number of days in the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine` TIMES `the part of the penalty paid`) DIVIDED BY `the total penalty`)

-- (3): the bar on accepting a part payment after the warrant is executed unless it secures a whole number of days, and before the fee is paid.
-- src:15740 | Minimum that can be accepted
-- src:15741 | (3) No amount offered in part payment of a penalty shall be accepted after the execution of a warrant of committal unless it is sufficient to secure a reduction of sentence of one day, or a whole number multiple of one day, and no part payment shall be accepted until any fee that is payable in respect of the warrant or its execution has been paid.
@ref s 734.8(3) (src:15740-15741)
GIVEN `the warrant of committal has been executed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction of sentence that the amount offered would secure, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the fee payable in respect of the warrant or its execution has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.8(3) acceptance of the part payment is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the fee payable in respect of the warrant or its execution has been paid` THEN JUST TRUE   -- gate: the text closes it with "no part payment shall be accepted until"
        IF `the warrant of committal has been executed` AND ((`the reduction of sentence that the amount offered would secure, in days` LESS THAN 1) OR (NOT (`the reduction of sentence that the amount offered would secure, in days` EQUALS FLOOR `the reduction of sentence that the amount offered would secure, in days`))) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No amount offered in part payment of a penalty shall be accepted after the execution of a warrant of committal unless it is sufficient to secure a reduction of sentence of one day, or a whole number multiple of one day"

-- src:15742 | To whom payment made
-- src:15743 | (4) Payment may be made under this section to the person that the Attorney General directs or, if the offender is imprisoned, to the person who has lawful custody of the prisoner or to any other person that the Attorney General directs.
@ref s 734.8(4) (src:15742-15743)
GIVEN `the Attorney General directs the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is imprisoned and the person has lawful custody of the prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734.8(4) payment may be made to the person` MEANS   -- gate: none (the persons are listed; the list is not closed with "only")
    IF `the Attorney General directs the person` OR `the offender is imprisoned and the person has lawful custody of the prisoner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Payment may be made under this section to the person that the Attorney General directs or, if the offender is imprisoned, to the person who has lawful custody of the prisoner or to any other person that the Attorney General directs"

-- (5): the order in which a payment is applied: costs and charges, then the victim surcharge under section 737, then the fine.
-- src:15744 | Application of money paid
-- src:15745 | (5) A payment under this section shall be applied firstly to the payment in full of costs and charges, secondly to the payment in full of any victim surcharge imposed under section 737, and then to payment of any part of the fine that remains unpaid.
@ref s 734.8(5) (src:15744-15745)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs and charges unpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 734.8(5) the part of the payment applied firstly to the costs and charges` MEANS
    IF `the payment` AT MOST `the costs and charges unpaid` THEN `the payment` ELSE `the costs and charges unpaid`

@ref s 734.8(5) (src:15744-15745)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs and charges unpaid` IS A NUMBER
      `the victim surcharge imposed under section 737 unpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 734.8(5) the part of the payment applied secondly to the victim surcharge imposed under section 737` MEANS
    IF (`the payment` MINUS (`s 734.8(5) the part of the payment applied firstly to the costs and charges` `the payment` `the costs and charges unpaid`)) AT MOST `the victim surcharge imposed under section 737 unpaid`
    THEN `the payment` MINUS (`s 734.8(5) the part of the payment applied firstly to the costs and charges` `the payment` `the costs and charges unpaid`)
    ELSE `the victim surcharge imposed under section 737 unpaid`

@ref s 734.8(5) (src:15744-15745)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs and charges unpaid` IS A NUMBER
      `the victim surcharge imposed under section 737 unpaid` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the fine that remains unpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 734.8(5) the part of the payment applied then to the part of the fine that remains unpaid` MEANS
    IF ((`the payment` MINUS (`s 734.8(5) the part of the payment applied firstly to the costs and charges` `the payment` `the costs and charges unpaid`)) MINUS (`s 734.8(5) the part of the payment applied secondly to the victim surcharge imposed under section 737` `the payment` `the costs and charges unpaid` `the victim surcharge imposed under section 737 unpaid`)) AT MOST `the part of the fine that remains unpaid`
    THEN (`the payment` MINUS (`s 734.8(5) the part of the payment applied firstly to the costs and charges` `the payment` `the costs and charges unpaid`)) MINUS (`s 734.8(5) the part of the payment applied secondly to the victim surcharge imposed under section 737` `the payment` `the costs and charges unpaid` `the victim surcharge imposed under section 737 unpaid`)
    ELSE `the part of the fine that remains unpaid`

§ `Section 735 -- Fines on organizations`

-- src:15746 | Fines on organizations
-- src:15747 | 735 (1) An organization that is convicted of an offence is liable, in lieu of any imprisonment that is prescribed as punishment for that offence, to be fined in an amount, except where otherwise provided by law,
-- src:15748 | (a) that is in the discretion of the court, where the offence is an indictable offence; or
-- src:15749 | (b) not exceeding one hundred thousand dollars, where the offence is a summary conviction offence.
@ref s 735(1) (src:15746-15749)
`s 735(1)(b) one hundred thousand dollars` MEANS 100000

@ref s 735(1) (src:15746-15749)
GIVEN `the person is an organization that is convicted of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is proceeded with by` IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `the amount of the fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 735(1) the organization is liable to be fined in the amount, in lieu of any imprisonment prescribed` MEANS   -- gate: none (the limits are on who, and the ceiling on a summary conviction offence); "except where otherwise provided by law" is not computed
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is an organization that is convicted of an offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An organization that is convicted of an offence is liable"
        IF `the offence is proceeded with by` EQUALS `by indictment` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the amount of the fine` AT MOST `s 735(1)(b) one hundred thousand dollars` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "not exceeding one hundred thousand dollars, where the offence is a summary conviction offence"

-- src:15750 | Application of certain provisions — fines
-- src:15751 | (1.1) A court that imposes a fine under subsection (1) or under any other Act of Parliament shall make an order that clearly sets out
-- src:15752 | (a) the amount of the fine;
-- src:15753 | (b) the manner in which the fine is to be paid;
-- src:15754 | (c) the time or times by which the fine, or any portion of it, must be paid; and
-- src:15755 | (d) any other terms respecting the payment of the fine that the court deems appropriate.
@ref s 735(1.1) (src:15750-15755)
GIVEN `the court imposes a fine under subsection 735(1) or under any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order clearly sets out the amount of the fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order clearly sets out the manner in which the fine is to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order clearly sets out the time or times by which the fine, or any portion of it, must be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court deems other terms respecting the payment of the fine appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order clearly sets out those other terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 735(1.1) the order clearly sets out the terms the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court imposes a fine under subsection 735(1) or under any other Act of Parliament` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that imposes a fine under subsection (1) or under any other Act of Parliament shall make an order"
        IF `the order clearly sets out the amount of the fine` AND `the order clearly sets out the manner in which the fine is to be paid` AND `the order clearly sets out the time or times by which the fine, or any portion of it, must be paid` AND ((NOT `the court deems other terms respecting the payment of the fine appropriate`) OR `the order clearly sets out those other terms`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall make an order that clearly sets out (a) the amount of the fine; (b) the manner in which the fine is to be paid; (c) the time or times by which the fine, or any portion of it, must be paid; and (d) any other terms respecting the payment of the fine that the court deems appropriate"

-- src:15756 | Effect of filing order
-- src:15757 | (2) Section 734.6 applies, with any modifications that are required, when an organization fails to pay the fine in accordance with the terms of the order.
@ref s 735(2) (src:15756-15757)
GIVEN `an organization fails to pay the fine in accordance with the terms of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 735(2) section 734.6 applies` MEANS
    IF `an organization fails to pay the fine in accordance with the terms of the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 734.6 applies, with any modifications that are required, when an organization fails to pay the fine in accordance with the terms of the order"

§ `Section 736 -- Fine option program`

-- 736(1): "may ... discharge the fine ... by earning credits for work performed during a period not greater than two years in a program established ... (a) of the province in which
-- the fine was imposed, or (b) of the province in which the offender resides, where an appropriate agreement is in effect, ... if the offender is admissible to such a program".
-- src:15758 | Fine option program
-- src:15759 | 736 (1) An offender who is fined under section 734 may, whether or not the offender is serving a term of imprisonment imposed in default of payment of the fine, discharge the fine in whole or in part by earning credits for work performed during a period not greater than two years in a program established for that purpose by the lieutenant governor in council
-- src:15760 | (a) of the province in which the fine was imposed, or
-- src:15761 | (b) of the province in which the offender resides, where an appropriate agreement is in effect between the government of that province and the government of the province in which the fine was imposed,
-- src:15762 | if the offender is admissible to such a program.
@ref s 736(1) (src:15758-15762)
GIVEN `the offender is fined under section 734` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the program is established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the fine was imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the program is established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the offender resides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appropriate agreement is in effect between the government of the province in which the offender resides and the government of the province in which the fine was imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is admissible to such a program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period during which the work is performed` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 736(1) the offender may discharge the fine in whole or in part by earning credits for work performed in the program` MEANS   -- gate: where (an appropriate agreement is in effect, for the program of the province in which the offender resides), if (the offender is admissible to such a program)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offender is fined under section 734` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An offender who is fined under section 734 may"
        IF `the program is established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the offender resides` AND (NOT `the program is established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the fine was imposed`) AND (NOT `an appropriate agreement is in effect between the government of the province in which the offender resides and the government of the province in which the fine was imposed`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) of the province in which the offender resides, where an appropriate agreement is in effect between the government of that province and the government of the province in which the fine was imposed"
        IF NOT (`the program is established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the fine was imposed` OR `the program is established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the offender resides`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a program established for that purpose by the lieutenant governor in council (a) of the province in which the fine was imposed, or (b) of the province in which the offender resides"
        IF NOT `the offender is admissible to such a program` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the offender is admissible to such a program"
        IF `s 716 the first period is at most the second period` `the period during which the work is performed` `two years` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for work performed during a period not greater than two years"

-- 736(2) (the program sets the rate of credits) is machinery (inert, reason 2).
-- src:15765 | Deemed payment
-- src:15766 | (3) Credits earned for work performed as provided by subsection (1) shall, for the purposes of this Act, be deemed to be payment in respect of a fine.
@ref s 736(3) (src:15765-15766)
GIVEN `credits are earned for work performed as provided by subsection 736(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 736(3) the credits are deemed to be payment in respect of a fine` MEANS
    IF `credits are earned for work performed as provided by subsection 736(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Credits earned for work performed as provided by subsection (1) shall, for the purposes of this Act, be deemed to be payment in respect of a fine"

-- src:15767 | Federal-provincial agreement
-- src:15768 | (4) Where, by virtue of subsection 734.4(2), the proceeds of a fine belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada, an offender may discharge the fine in whole or in part in a fine option program of a province pursuant to subsection (1), where an appropriate agreement is in effect between the government of the province and the Government of Canada.
@ref s 736(4) (src:15767-15768)
GIVEN `the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada by virtue of subsection 734.4(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appropriate agreement is in effect between the government of the province and the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 736(4) the offender may discharge the fine in whole or in part in a fine option program of a province` MEANS   -- gate: where (the proceeds belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada), where (an appropriate agreement is in effect between the province and Canada)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceeds of the fine belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada by virtue of subsection 734.4(2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, by virtue of subsection 734.4(2), the proceeds of a fine belong to Her Majesty in right of Canada, an offender may discharge the fine"
        IF NOT `an appropriate agreement is in effect between the government of the province and the Government of Canada` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an appropriate agreement is in effect between the government of the province and the Government of Canada"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
